            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-KozydEEvzoktnexjyMXl6fKUgQg\">Looking at the countries with continuous population growth, in 2003, Indonesia's figure of 238 million was significantly higher than that of Argentina, at just 34 million. The population of Argentina is forecast to almost double by 2050, reaching 62 million, while Indonesia's numbers are predicted to rise by nearly one-third to 312 million.</div>\n</div>",
